  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "tap-rtspstat: improve memory management",
  "description": "Add a finish function to the call of `register_tap_listener()` which\nfrees the memory allocated by the tap. This includes the tap data\nallocated upon registration, as well as the `GHashTable`s holding\nrequest and response statistics.\n\nReplace `g_hash_table_new()` calls with `g_hash_table_new_full()` to\nprovide callback functions for freeing the keys and values of hash\nentries as they are being removed.\n\n* The keys for `hash_responses` are numbers stored using\n  `GINT_TO_POINTER()` so no callback is needed. The values are created\n  with `g_new()` so `g_free` is a sufficient callback.\n* The keys for `hash_requests` are strings, which are also pointed to by\n  the a member of the `g_new()`-allocated values. `g_free` as the\n  callback for both the key and value takes care of it, but this may be\n  non-obvious for future maintainers.\n\nPing #20432",
